course: dictionary
lesson: 10651
title: Unite and united
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To unite means to join together to make one group or one thing. «The two clubs united.» The clubs became one team, so unite means join together.
explain: To unite people means to bring them together so they work for the same goal. «Temujin united the Mongol tribes» means he brought separate tribes together so they could work as one people. United can also be an adjective, meaning joined together or agreeing: «united we stand».
explain: Look at the words around unite to check its meaning. Phrases such as «unite against» and «unite behind» show what the joining is for. In «people unite against a danger», the word against is a clue that the people joined together to face something bad.
fact: To unite means to join together to make one group or one thing.
fact: United can be a verb (they united) or an adjective (a united team).
fact: Phrases like «unite against» and «unite behind» tell you what people are joining for.
fact: «United we stand» is a saying meaning that people are stronger when they work together.
fact: In 221 BC «the state of Qin united» China, and it made writing and coins the same everywhere, but it also used forced labour, so uniting does not always mean kind.
exercise: «The two clubs united.» What does united mean here? | Split apart into two groups | Lost every game they played | Went home early | *Joined together to make one group
exercise: In «Temujin united the Mongol tribes», what did he do? | Fought every tribe he met | *Brought the separate tribes together so they worked as one | Forgot their names | Split the tribes into smaller groups
exercise: In «a united team», what kind of word is united? | A question word | *An adjective | A verb | A noun
test: «The villagers unite against the flood.» What does unite against mean? | Run away from the flood | *Join together to face the flood | Ask someone else to fix it | Build a boat on their own
test: «In 221 BC the state of Qin united China.» What does united mean here? | *The separate states were joined into one country | China was split into rival states | The states started a war with each other | China was painted in new colours
exam: Which sentence uses united as an adjective? | They unite every time there is a danger | The clubs united last spring | Temujin united the tribes in 1206 | *The united family agreed on the plan
